<title>THAILAND: Thailand awards three bank licences to old groups.</title>
<headline>Thailand awards three bank licences to old groups.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance Minister Amnuay Viravan said on Friday the new coalition government of Prime Minister Chavalit Yongchaiyudh would follow a decision by its predecessor in granting new Thai bank licences to three local consortia.</p>
<p>Amnuay said the three licence winners are groups led by Italian-Thai Development Plc, General Finance and Securities Plc, and MBK Properties and Development Plc.</p>
</text>
